# Ent Hooks & Interceptors

## 1. Schema Hooks (Mutation Hooks)

Hooks defined in the schema run during mutation operations (Create, Update, Delete).

```go
// ent/schema/user.go
func (User) Hooks() []ent.Hook {
    return []ent.Hook{
        OnUserUpdate(),
    }
}

func OnUserUpdate() ent.Hook {
    return func(next ent.Mutator) ent.Mutator {
        return ent.MutateFunc(func(ctx context.Context, m ent.Mutation) (ent.Value, error) {
            // Pre-mutation logic
            if !m.Op().Is(ent.OpUpdate | ent.OpUpdateOne) {
                return next.Mutate(ctx, m)
            }
            
            // Access fields
            if name, exists := m.Field("name"); exists {
                fmt.Printf("Updating name to %s\n", name)
            }

            // Call next mutator (database operation)
            v, err := next.Mutate(ctx, m)

            // Post-mutation logic
            if err == nil {
                fmt.Println("Update success")
            }
            
            return v, err
        })
    }
}
```

### Hook Registration
- **Schema-level:** Defined in `func (T) Hooks()`. Runs only for that entity.
- **Runtime-level:** `client.User.Use(MyHook)`.

## 2. Interceptors (Query Interceptors)

Intercept Read/Query operations.

```go
// ent/schema/user.go
func (User) Interceptors() []ent.Interceptor {
    return []ent.Interceptor{
        ent.InterceptFunc(func(next ent.Querier) ent.Querier {
            return ent.QuerierFunc(func(ctx context.Context, q ent.Query) (ent.Value, error) {
                // Filter Soft-deleted users globally
                if query, ok := q.(*ent.UserQuery); ok {
                    query.Where(user.DeletedAtIsNil())
                }
                return next.Query(ctx, q)
            })
        }),
    }
}
```

## 3. Global Hooks (Runtime)

Register hooks for all operations on the client.

```go
// main.go or setup
client.Use(func(next ent.Mutator) ent.Mutator {
    return ent.MutateFunc(func(ctx context.Context, m ent.Mutation) (ent.Value, error) {
        start := time.Now()
        v, err := next.Mutate(ctx, m)
        log.Printf("Op: %s, Type: %s, Duration: %s", m.Op(), m.Type(), time.Since(start))
        return v, err
    })
})
```

## 4. Helper Functions

Use `ent.Op` to filter operations inside hooks.

```go
if m.Op().Is(ent.OpCreate) { ... }
if m.Op().Is(ent.OpDelete | ent.OpDeleteOne) { ... }
```

